{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QuarkState.ConePointChiralityBit","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QuarkState.ConePointChiralityBit","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QuarkState.OneSidedWeakVertex","lean:module:QOU.StandardModel.ChiralityPolarizationHopf"],"declarations":15,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.ConePointBit.const_assignment_equivariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.ConePointBit.const_assignment_equivariant","kind":"theorem","line":168,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/ConePointChiralityBit.lean#L168-L178","doc":"**Non-vacuity**: a constant assignment (a fixed convention, `ρ = id`, one letter `s`)\nsatisfies both equivariance hypotheses. So the theorem says that the equivariant\nassignments are exactly the ones that ignore which line `u` calls left-handed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.ConePointBit.cone_point_cannot_pick_bit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.ConePointBit.cone_point_cannot_pick_bit","kind":"theorem","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/ConePointChiralityBit.lean#L151-L165","doc":"**The cone point cannot pick the L/R bit equivariantly.** For any letter field `ℓ` on\nthe cone and any assignment `τ` that is equivariant under the unit-quaternion gauge (acting\non `u` by conjugation and on the algebra by any `K`-algebra maps `ρ g`), the vertex type\nat `u = i` equals the type at its antipode `−i`, which `chiralGammaU_neg` identifies as the\nphoton swap `Γ ↦ −Γ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.ConePointBit.normSq_unitJ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.ConePointBit.normSq_unitJ","kind":"theorem","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/ConePointChiralityBit.lean#L146-L147","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.ConePointBit.conjBy_unitJ_unitI","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.ConePointBit.conjBy_unitJ_unitI","kind":"theorem","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/ConePointChiralityBit.lean#L142-L144","doc":"Conjugation by the unit `j` sends the chirality point `u = i` to its antipode `−i`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.ConePointBit.type_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.ConePointBit.type_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/ConePointChiralityBit.lean#L123-L132","doc":"**An equivariant type assignment is constant along gauge orbits.** `act` is any action\nof `G` on points, and `ρ g` any `K`-algebra endomorphism (the trivial one included). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.ConePointBit.vertex_inj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.ConePointBit.vertex_inj","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/ConePointChiralityBit.lean#L117-L121","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.ConePointBit.map_vertex","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.ConePointBit.map_vertex","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/ConePointChiralityBit.lean#L113-L115","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.ConePointBit.vertex","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.ConePointBit.vertex","kind":"def","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/ConePointChiralityBit.lean#L108-L110","doc":"The vertex of type `b` (`true` = L-only, `false` = R-only). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.ConePointBit.oneSidedL_ne_oneSidedR","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.ConePointBit.oneSidedL_ne_oneSidedR","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/ConePointChiralityBit.lean#L81-L99","doc":"The two one-sided flips differ unless `q² = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.ConePointBit.map_oneSidedR","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.ConePointBit.map_oneSidedR","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/ConePointChiralityBit.lean#L71-L72","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.ConePointBit.map_oneSidedL","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.ConePointBit.map_oneSidedL","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/ConePointChiralityBit.lean#L67-L69","doc":"**Algebra maps preserve the L-only type.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.ConePointBit.map_isLetter","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.ConePointBit.map_isLetter","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/ConePointChiralityBit.lean#L63-L65","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.ConePointBit.map_flip","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.ConePointBit.map_flip","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/ConePointChiralityBit.lean#L60-L61","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.ConePointBit.map_Pm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.ConePointBit.map_Pm","kind":"theorem","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/ConePointChiralityBit.lean#L57-L58","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuarkState.ConePointBit.map_Pp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuarkState.ConePointBit.map_Pp","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuarkState/ConePointChiralityBit.lean#L54-L55","signatureChunk":0}]}